## Component Name

**Path**: [src/components/OmronE5Types.h](../src/components/OmronE5Types.h)

**Revision History**:
- 2023-10-20: Initial documentation

A component interface for Omron E5 temperature controllers using Modbus-485 communication protocol. Defines register addresses, status bits, commands, and error codes for communication with Omron E5 devices.

## Requirements

### Dependencies
- RS485 communication module
- Modbus protocol implementation

### Configuration
```c
// Enable Omron E5 controllers in config.h
#define ENABLE_OMRON_E5
#define NUM_OMRON_DEVICES 1          // Number of connected Omron E5 devices
#define OMRON_E5_SLAVE_ID_BASE 1     // Base Modbus slave ID
```

## Features

- Comprehensive register mapping for Omron E5 controllers
- Status bit definitions for monitoring controller state
- Command definitions for controlling the device 
- Support for reading PV (Process Values), SP (Set Points), and other parameters
- Support for multiple Omron E5 devices on the same bus
- Error handling for communication issues

## Todos

- Add support for additional E5 series models
- Implement profile temperature control
- Add callback functions for status changes

## Example

```c
// Adding an Omron E5 controller to your components list
#ifdef ENABLE_OMRON_E5
  for (uint8_t i = 0; i < NUM_OMRON_DEVICES; i++)
  {
    uint8_t slaveId = OMRON_E5_SLAVE_ID_BASE + i;
    OmronE5* omronDevice = new OmronE5(
      this,                 // owner
      slaveId,              // Modbus slave ID
      100 + i               // component ID
    );

    if (omronDevice)
    {
      components.push_back(omronDevice);
      Log.infoln(F("Omron E5 controller initialized. ID:%d, Slave ID:%d"),
                 100 + i, slaveId);
    }
    else
    {
      Log.errorln(F("Omron E5 controller initialization failed."));
    }
  }
#endif
```"}

